{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1449541-running-a-beast-court-garou-nation-game-in-the-philippines","id":1449541,"title":"Running a Beast Court/Garou Nation game in the Philippines.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-25T05:05:06-07:00","id":1449541,"title":"Running a Beast Court/Garou Nation game in the Philippines.","content":"Planning to run a WTA game once my current VTM game is done.<br /> <br /> currently my idea is that the native Bone Gnawers were responsible for the weredog variants of the Aswang.<br /> <br /> But i need to flesh this out more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25313-raziel","name":"Raziel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T13:47:02-07:00","id":1449581,"title":"","content":"Nice. I've run a lot of similar campaigns set in Indo/Malaysia.<br /> <br /> Not sure about Sigbin being Garou....they have some very non-Garou traits. Both Pinoy and Indo tradition have were-pigs as well which tempted me to make them remnant Grondr but they come of more as Sorcerers in folklore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T18:51:51-07:00","id":1449598,"title":"","content":"Maybe some sort of obscure surviving Grondr kinfolk bloodline who have an affinity for shapeshifting magic?<br /> <br /> I suppose the Aswang could be either a breed of fomori or the subculture of Filipino vampires (whose Protean forms are black dogs or boars instead of wolves, and either bats or whatever bird the tiktik is supposed to be). <br /> <br /> There's also the Sarangay, which physically resembles the minotaur in some ways. If such a thing still existed in the islands, it might be one of the last remnants of the Apis or something. <br /> <br /> The Beast Courts in the Philippines are probably primarily influenced by the Chinese courts. I'd guess a Glass Walker and Bone Gnawer presence in Manila and other large cities. Maybe other tribes in select numbers as the result of various waves of immigration over the centuries. The Mokole are probably primarily the East Asian stream, but you may also have some of the Indian and possibly even a few isolated Australian ones here and there. Certainly a relatively fair number of Nagah. Ratkin. I think the only native cats are small ones, but I may be mistaken. Ananasi and Rokea.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T19:40:15-07:00","id":1449608,"title":"","content":"Aswang is a very broad term, in WoD speak its like saying Night Folk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T00:46:39-07:00","id":1449770,"title":"","content":"I had to read up on Philippine wildlife before I could respond. If my understanding is correct, the Philippine islands seem to lack the typical large carnivorous predators that form the basis for much of the werebeast legends. So I think ant WtA game set there will rely on a lot of speculation and personal taste.<br /> <br /> There's probably some Mokole there, and they have Corvids so Corax could be justified. Since the Philippines don't seem ever to have wolves, big cats, large bears, etc. they likely missed out entirely on the War of Rage. Spiders are also everywhere, so there could be Ananasi. They have rodents though the black and brown rats are invasive species not native there, so maybe not any native Ratkin but they might have arrived later. And of course the Rokea would be in nearby waters.<br /> <br /> As for Garou, any would have arrived far later making them relative newcomers. I am not familiar with the stories of Aswang weredogs, but I think we should keep &quot;dogs&quot; in perspective. Since there are no native wolves, anyone seeing a canid-like creature might have received the name &quot;dog&quot;. Bone Gnawers aren't dogs either, they are still wolves. So any number of tribes (including more than one) might be responsible for the legend.<br /> <br /> Wikipedia tells me the Aswang weredog eats people and avoids marrying into the community, arriving as a travelling peddler or laborer. A propensity of man eating is best known among Bone Gnawers, but Silent Striders and others do as well. And the travelling aspect suits Silent Striders. The weredogs are often seen as black, which associates with Shadow Lords and Black Furies. On one other web page I read, it says that Aswangs in general (going beyond the weredogs to other monsters) often take female form. That might point towards some Black Furies, likely far travelling freebooters.<br /> <br /> If I was going to design a Rage Across the Philippines chronicle, I think I'd say that the first Garou to arrive there (likely quite some time after the War of Rage, maybe around the start of the Common Era but perhaps not until Chinese ships began exploring the area in 9th/10th centuries) were those Garou most likely to travel far and explore - Silent Striders and Black Furies. They may have started a &quot;native&quot; branch of Garou. Both are known to interbreed a lot and not be picky.<br /> <br /> Then when the Spanish arrived in the 16th century, other Garou might have eventually arrived - any tribes that make sense to you from Iberia. That might include Spanish Fianna, Get, or Shadow Lords. And Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers also become possible as Manila develops.<br /> <br /> Werebeast legends in general often include man eating, but the game has always downplayed it. So it's still up to you whether this is a serious problem for the Garou, or represents something else like cannibalistic Black Spiral Dancers or some kind of fomori.<br /> <br /> I personally would not associate them with the Beast Courts of China. While there has been a long Overseas Chinese presence in the Philippines for a while, the islands have never really been part of the Sinocentric world. But I would encourage unique local takes and alliances as a result of these islands likely missing out of the War of Rage and all the baggage that has. They might have some sort of unique &quot;Beast Court&quot; of their own representing local flavor, although I would use a different term so that any kind of alliance would be distinct from the other one. Maybe something like The Children of the Islands. The &quot;native&quot; Garou might be included in that, but not the Garou tribes who arrived with the Spanish. Maybe they might look to the Silver Fangs of Australia for the closest &quot;leadership&quot; of the Nation. That could make some interesting tribal politics.<br /> <br /> Hope my speculations provide some inspiration of other help for you in designing your chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}